BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Goatlandia invites the Community to "Reggae to the Rescue!"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T170000
UID:260813FQbe6LjGUU-EdmnwE-zJNQ
DESCRIPTION:**Party with a Purpose: Goatlandia Invites the Community to "R
 eggae to the Rescue"—An Afternoon of Music\, Compassion & Farm Animal Fu
 n**\n\n*Sonoma County's favorite reggae band\, Sol Horizon\, headlines Goa
 tlandia's biggest "fun-raising" celebration of the year on Saturday\, Augu
 st 22.FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE*\n\n**SEBASTOPOL\, Calif. —** Goatlandia Far
 m Animal Sanctuary & Education Center invites the community to trade the t
 raditional black-tie gala for ﬂip-ﬂops\, island colors\, and good vibe
 s at **Reggae to the Rescue**\, its annual fundraising celebration\, on **
 Saturday\, August 22\, 2026**\, from **1:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.** at the san
 ctuary's beautiful 36-acre property in Sebastopol. VIP guests are welcomed
  from **1:00–2:00 p.m.**\, with General Admission beginning at **2:00 p.
 m.** and continuing through **5:00 p.m.** The event brings together live m
 usic\, rescued farm animals\, delicious food and drinks\, and a shared com
 mitment to creating a more compassionate world. Event details are availabl
 e at https://www.goatlandia.org/events/reggae-to-the-rescue.\n\nHeadlining
  this year's celebration is **Sol Horizon**\, Sonoma County's beloved regg
 ae band\, whose uplifting performances and loyal local following make them
  the perfect soundtrack for an unforgettable afternoon of community and co
 mpassion. Guests will enjoy tropical-inspired food from Goatlandia Kitchen
 \, local beverages\, time with the sanctuary's rescued animal residents\, 
 games\, auctions\, and the joyful atmosphere that has become a hallmark of
  Goatlandia's annual fundraising events.\n\nUnlike traditional fundraising
  galas\, Goatlandia's annual celebration is intentionally designed to be w
 elcoming\, relaxed\, and accessible.\n\n"Last year's theme was *Peace\, Lo
 ve & Goats*\, and the response from our community reminded us that people 
 are looking for meaningful ways to come together\," said **Deborah Blum**\
 , founder of Goatlandia. "With *Reggae to the*\n\n*Rescue*\, we're celebra
 ting compassion\, community\, and second chances—for animals and for peo
 ple. We wanted to create a fundraiser that feels more like a joyful party 
 than a formal gala\, where everyone can be part of making a diﬀerence wh
 ile dancing\, laughing\, and spending time with our rescued animals. We ar
 e so grateful to our incredible community for making this work possible."\
 n\nProceeds from Reggae to the Rescue directly support Goatlandia's rescue
 \, rehabilitation\, and lifelong care of farm animals while helping expand
  the organization's education programs that inspire kindness toward animal
 s\, people\, and the planet. The sanctuary has become a beloved destinatio
 n for families\, volunteers\, and visitors from throughout Northern Califo
 rnia seeking meaningful experiences that connect compassion with action.\n
 \nGuests are encouraged to wear their brightest island attire\, bring frie
 nds and family\, and join Goatlandia for an afternoon where every ticket h
 elps provide food\, shelter\, veterinary care\, and hope for rescued farm 
 animals.\n\nFor tickets and event information\, visit\n\n**https://www.goa
 tlandia.org/events/reggae-to-the-rescue**.\n\n About Goatlandia Farm Anim
 al Sanctuary & Education Center\n\nGoatlandia is a nonproﬁt farm animal 
 sanctuary in Sebastopol\, California\, dedicated to rescuing farm animals\
 , inspiring compassionate choices\, and creating meaningful connections be
 tween animals\, people\, and the planet. Through rescue\, education\, comm
 unity events\, and hands-on experiences\, Goatlandia provides a safe haven
  for animals while empowering people to live with greater kindness and pur
 pose.\n\nMedia Contact\n\nDeborah Blum\n\nFounder\, Goatlandia Farm Animal
  Sanctuary & Education Center Email: **deborah@goatlandia.org**\n\nPhone: 
 **(707) 541-6216**\n\nWebsite: **https://www.goatlandia.org**
LOCATION:Goatlandia Farm Animal Sanctuary and Education Center 
URL:https://www.goatlandia.org/events/reggae-to-the-rescue
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sgt. Splendor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T000000
UID:2608136xGL0JF-MU6-rGbjPSTj6Q
DESCRIPTION:Before joining forces\, the duo behind Sgt. Splendor were alre
 ady formidable solo artists\, Kate Vargas chalking up acclaim at outlets l
 ike NPR\, SPIN\, and Vice \\(including praise from the “Dean of American
  Rock Critics” Robert Christgau\\)\; and Eric McFadden amassing an impre
 ssive resume including stints on guitar with George Clinton & the P-Funk A
 ll Stars\, Fishbone’s Angelo Moore\, and Eric Burdon & The Animals\, plu
 s a slew of solo albums\, and session work with everyone from Jackson Brow
 ne to The Clash’s Joe Strummer.\n\nSgt. Splendor’s intoxicating chemis
 try on the new album has its roots not just in enduring friendships\, but 
 also in the love and connection of its creative partners\, Vargas and McFa
 dden. After circling each other’s orbits for a time\, they finally met a
 t a songwriting retreat hosted by Pat MacDonald \\(of Timbuk 3 / “Future
 ’s So Bright I Gotta Wear Shades” fame\\) in Sturgeon Bay\, WI\, initi
 ally bonding over yet another parallel\, a New Mexico upbringing. Their So
 uthwestern roots upbringing come through with Sgt. Splendor—combining my
 sterioso desert and carnivalesque Waits-ian vibe.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108625931?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
