BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Josh Flores: Big Feels - Featured August Artist in the Living Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T170000
UID:260804v8VYphSljE2x0pO34zCHsA
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents the 
 artwork of **Josh Flores** in the Living Room of the Maurice Del Mue Gal
 leries. There will be a reception for the artist on **August 9 from 2 - 4
  pm**. \n\nJosh has previously exhibited work in the San Rafael Youth In 
 Arts Program  “What About Age?” exhibit at the Marin Civic Center and
  the “One If By Land\, Two if By Sea” show at the Bolinas Art Museum.
  This is Josh’s first solo exhibition at the Community Center.\n\n**Art
 ist bio:** Josh Flores was born in Lima\, Peru and raised in Marin. He ap
 preciates the experience of taking a blank piece of paper and going throug
 h the process of making something as a reminder to himself that he is capa
 ble of anything. His earliest influence to make art came from watching ama
 teur anime\, reading manga and his first art teacher Mr. Powell.\n\n**Arti
 st statement:** Titled “BIG Feels” the inspiration for his first solo
  show came from his recent birthday\, when he experienced emotional sadnes
 s related to fear of abandonment. He created the first piece titled “Sad
  Boi Birthday” to illustrate the depth of the emotion he was feeling. Ea
 ch piece is created with a graphite sketch followed by ink and alcohol mar
 ker.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/josh-flo
 res-big-feels-featured-august-artist-in-the-living-room
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T170000
UID:260803ocPhvUurR0C-WQzBAwg0Pg
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pages & Pours: Reading in a Wine Cave at Joseph Cellars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T153000
UID:260803hRNPFXKcbUGu17SHu7mcsw
DESCRIPTION:**Pages & Pours at Joseph Cellars — Escape the Heat\, Sink I
 nto a Book**\n\nIt's August. It's hot. And you've probably been trying to 
 finish the same book for weeks.\n\nPages & Pours gives you an afternoon wh
 ere reading is the only thing on your to-do list.\n\nJoin Novel Pairings f
 or an afternoon in the wine cave at Joseph Cellars on Sunday\, August 23 f
 rom 1–3:30pm\, one of the coolest\, quietest rooms in Napa Valley on a s
 ummer afternoon. Bring whatever you're currently reading\, whether it's a 
 thriller\, a romance\, or something you've been stuck on for a month. Star
 t with a short tasting to find the wine that fits your book and your mood\
 , then settle into the cave for dedicated reading time. It's the kind of a
 fternoon that's hard to carve out on your own\, so we're doing it for you.
 \n\n**No assigned book. No discussion required. No pressure to perform.**\
 n\nWhen the reading winds down\, there's an optional book swap\, a chance 
 to mingle\, and space to read aloud the line that stopped you in your trac
 ks\, if you're up for it.\n\nAnd since you've already made the drive up fr
 om the Bay\, why turn around right away? The event wraps at 3:30\, leaving
  you a full Napa Valley afternoon ahead of you: Calistoga's shops and hot 
 springs\, a stop at another winery\, or an early dinner before the trip ho
 me.\n\nTickets are $20 for Novel Pairings and Joseph Cellars Club members\
 , $30 general admission\, less than a typical brunch for an afternoon of u
 ninterrupted reading\, wine\, and quiet. Each ticket includes the tasting 
 and one glass of Joseph Cellars wine.\n\n**Sunday\, August 23 · 1–3:30p
 m · Joseph Cellars\, 4455 St. Helena Hwy N.\, Calistoga\, CA**
LOCATION:Joseph Cellars
URL:https://www.novel-pairings.com/pagespourscalistoga
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
