BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mokuhanga (Ukiyo-e) Japanese Woodblock Printmaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T160000
UID:260728vCAfz8crCkmnWuLPwvAhbA
DESCRIPTION:Weekly every Sundays · 3 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 9 –
  23\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 4:00 PM Short lunch break included\n\nLocation\
 n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\
 nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$300\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$
 50\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$350\n\nIn this special three-part works
 hop\, participants will be introduced to the art of Japanese woodblock pri
 nting called Ukiyo-E technique. Tomoko Murakami\, an acclaimed Bay Area\, 
 Japanese-born printmaking artist\, will demonstrate the traditional Mokuha
 nga carving and printing process. Tomoko will introduce the relationship b
 etween positive and negative space in relief printing techniques\, includi
 ng Kento registration. Participants will learn to carve their own woodbloc
 ks using Japanese carving tools to create small multi-color woodblocks and
  create prints with non-toxic water-based inks on Japanese paper. Students
  will be able to develop an appreciation of Japanese woodblock prints\, ma
 terials\, processes and innovations. Learn to carve your own woodblocks an
 d create a small edition of multicolor prints! This class is perfect for b
 eginners as well as continuing students. All levels are welcome!Please not
 e: This class requires hand dexterity to maneuver the carving tools. Parti
 cipants should feel comfortable standing and using wood carving tools with
  sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/mokuhanga-japanese-woodbloc
 k-printmaking/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brazilian guitarist and composer Guinga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T200000
UID:260728n7mP-HzYjUKDP2Wyz0UjJg
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma Valley Jazz Society in partnership with the Sonoma 
 Petaluma Parks (SPPARKS) proud to present an intimate evening with interna
 tionally acclaimed Brazilian guitarist and composer **Guinga**\, performin
 g live at the historic **Sonoma Mission San Francisco Solano** on **Sunday
 \, August 23\, 2026\, at 6:30 PM**. Doors open at 6 PM.\n\nRecognized as o
 ne of Brazil’s most sophisticated and expressive musical voices\, Guinga
  has earned global admiration for his intricate harmonies\, lyrical depth\
 , and genre‑defying compositions that blend samba\, choro\, jazz\, and c
 lassical influences. His work has been recorded by legends including Elis 
 Regina\, Michel Legrand\, Chico Buarque\, and Clara Nunes.\n\nThis rare We
 st Coast appearance offers audiences a chance to experience Guinga’s art
 istry in one of Sonoma’s most iconic and intimate settings. The Mission
 ’s warm acoustics and historic character provide a perfect backdrop for 
 an evening of profound musical storytelling.\n\n“We are honored to bring
  an artist of Guinga’s stature to Sonoma\,” said Jonathan Hsu of  the
  Sonoma Valley Jazz Society. “His music is deeply emotional\, technicall
 y brilliant\, and unlike anything else in the world of contemporary guitar
 .”
LOCATION:Mission San Francisco Solano
URL:http://www.sonomavalleyjazzsociety.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Gathering
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T190000
UID:260728lvtUeFPm9kyNC22KeG2tXA
DESCRIPTION:Full Moon Gathering in honor of the Pisces Full Moon. 🌕\n\n
 This gathering takes place three days before the August lunation and focus
 es on building a relationship with the Moon through astrology\, art\, and 
 plants!\n\n🦂 Courtney Rae of Moonlight Floreciendo will lead a discussi
 on on the astrology of the Moon and practices for connecting with Luna\, i
 ncluding how to create a lunar tea.\n\n🌊 Jazz of Radical Wellness Colle
 ctive will offer thoughtful and creative prompts to guide your watercolor 
 creations\, as well as tea and snacks.\n\n🌿 Everyone will have the oppo
 rtunity to make a lunar tea blend with herbs from Sol Root and Growing Fut
 ures Vallejo.\n\nSliding scale tickets starting at $11.
LOCATION:Growing Futures Vallejo
URL:https://www.courtneyrae.online/event-details/radical-wellness-collecti
 ve-x-moonlight-floreciendo-presents-full-moon-gathering
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art of Community Festival - Youth Artists "Under 21"  Poetry Showc
 ase
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T160000
UID:260728ZFPPaE_Kx0qPtpCo18iczw
DESCRIPTION:We are proud to present the 3rd Annual Art of Community Festiv
 al\, a month-long celebration of creativity\, culture\, and community taki
 ng place throughout August on the historic Mare Island waterfront.\n\nWhat
  began as a grassroots community art exhibition has grown into a dynamic f
 estival that brings together artists\, youth creatives\, makers\, cultural
  organizations\, and community members in a shared celebration of the peop
 le and ideas that make Vallejo unique.\n\nBay Area artist Diana Krevsky's 
 exhibit "Legacy in Color" in the main gallery will be open all Sundays in 
 August. Krevsky’s work often explores the conflict between cultural valu
 es and individual identity within both political and natural landscapes. H
 er paintings and sculptures are at once colorful\, whimsical\, thought-pro
 voking\, and deeply personal. Visitors can meet the artist during the fest
 ival’s Opening Reception and Artist Talk Aug 8 at 2 p.m.\n\nAug 9\, Art 
 of Community Awards Honoring individuals and organizations making a meanin
 gful impact through art\, culture\, and community begins at 2 p.m.\n\nAug 
 16\, Mare Island Art • Fashion • Vintage Bazaar A waterfront market fe
 aturing artists\, makers\, fashion vendors\, vintage dealers\, collectors\
 , and creative entrepreneurs. $5 admission\n\nAug 23\, 2 to 4 p.m. Vallejo
  Youth Artists “Under 21” Exhibition Reception & Poetry Showcase Featu
 ring emerging artists and young creative voices from throughout the region
  begins at 2 p.m.
LOCATION:Mare Island Art Studios
URL:https://artiszen.org/bazaar
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
