DESCRIPTION:Inviting folks who support arts education to come out and enjo
 y interesting conversation and great food\, beverages\, and views as part 
 of the Sonoma County Arts Education Alliance! Attend the AEA Mixer to lear
 n more about what's going on in Sonoma County including the unveiling of t
 he Reggio Emilia Project Plan. Centered at the Sonoma County Office of Edu
 cation\, the Reggio project has already involved many arts\, education\, c
 ommunity\, and regional partners who are committed to creative\, respectfu
 l\, inquiry-based education for our youngest learners. Learn more about th
 e project so far  HERE . Teaching artists\, arts and cultural organization
 s\, arts and general education teachers\, school/district/county administr
 ators\, parents\, community advocates are ALL welcome! An extra special we
 lcome to Reggio Emilia Approach participants and supporters! \\(And if you
  don't know about Reggio\, come and find out more about this amazing proje
 ct!\\) Tuesday\, August 25\, 2026 from 4:30-6:30pm Waterhawk Lake Club\, 5
 000 Roberts Lake Rd.\, Rohnert Park No host bar. RSVP  HERE . Questions? D
 ebbie.Yarrow@sonomacounty.gov
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/arts-education-alliance-mixer/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
