DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T123000
UID:260805vryGA9y0VUilx2zvKfL0bw
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to preserve fresh produce through pickling and ferme
 ntation in this hands-on workshop. You’ll explore both vinegar-based and
  salt-based methods while making a variety of flavorful recipes.\n\nIn thi
 s workshop you’ll:\n\n• Learn the basics of fermentation and vinegar p
 ickling\n\n• Understand the differences between fermented\, fresh\, and 
 refrigerator pickles\n\n• Make 3 types of seasonal pickles and ferments\
 n\n• Learn how to safely store and continue pickling at home\n\nYou’ll
  leave with three jars of your own creations. All materials provided.
LOCATION:Gather Sebastopol
URL:https://gathersebastopol.com/products/preserve-the-season-intro-to-pic
 kling-and-fermentation
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Josh Flores: Big Feels - Featured August Artist in the Living Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T170000
UID:260804JeDNfSkoa0uRHzYkwPCQpw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents the 
 artwork of **Josh Flores** in the Living Room of the Maurice Del Mue Gal
 leries. There will be a reception for the artist on **August 9 from 2 - 4
  pm**. \n\nJosh has previously exhibited work in the San Rafael Youth In 
 Arts Program  “What About Age?” exhibit at the Marin Civic Center and
  the “One If By Land\, Two if By Sea” show at the Bolinas Art Museum.
  This is Josh’s first solo exhibition at the Community Center.\n\n**Art
 ist bio:** Josh Flores was born in Lima\, Peru and raised in Marin. He ap
 preciates the experience of taking a blank piece of paper and going throug
 h the process of making something as a reminder to himself that he is capa
 ble of anything. His earliest influence to make art came from watching ama
 teur anime\, reading manga and his first art teacher Mr. Powell.\n\n**Arti
 st statement:** Titled “BIG Feels” the inspiration for his first solo
  show came from his recent birthday\, when he experienced emotional sadnes
 s related to fear of abandonment. He created the first piece titled “Sad
  Boi Birthday” to illustrate the depth of the emotion he was feeling. Ea
 ch piece is created with a graphite sketch followed by ink and alcohol mar
 ker.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/josh-flo
 res-big-feels-featured-august-artist-in-the-living-room
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deep Dive into Soda Firing with Dan Clauson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T130000
UID:260803q7oE0CB9BkOGxamCwtq3dQ
DESCRIPTION:Tuesdays\, August 11 – September 1\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:
 00 PM\n\nWeekend Long Firing Workshop\n\nSaturday\, September 12\, 2026 10
 :00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nSunday\, September 13\, 2026 4:00 PM – 7:00 PM\n\n
 Location\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended 
 Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistrati
 on Cost:\n\n$320\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:
 \n\n$320\n\nIn this 4 session intensive\, students will create work for a 
 soda firing while learning the history and chemistry of atmospheric Soda. 
 Each session there will be demos and assignments that will lend to intenti
 onal and experimental decisions on the objects we make for the firing. We 
 will make tests in clay material\, slips\, glazes\, experiment in wadding\
 , and placements in the kiln. During class there will be lectures on the c
 hemistry of clay and of soda firing as well as its history\, application\,
  and experiments within the field. This class is about learning how to exp
 lore what soda can do.During the 4 weeks each student will create one cubi
 c foot of work to be bisqued and then fired in the soda kiln. The firing 
 will be two full days of activity\, with students applying the lessons lea
 rned in class to the wadding and loading of the kiln and lighting the kiln
 . Students will learn how to plan a gas kiln schedule\, use a kiln log\, a
 ssess a kilns needs\, and successfully fire off a kiln. Students will lear
 n how to spray soda and how to maintain the kiln and her accessories in or
 der to support Julia’s \\(our beloved soda kiln\\) longevity. This deep
  dive into soda will spark ideas and expand folx knowledge on kilns\, firi
 ng\, and making in clay.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/deep-dive-into-soda-firing-
 with-dan-clauson/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
