BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T193000
UID:2607049RaehBhh6U-dMmCpxDlFmg
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-08-25T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Expressions in Metal Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T000000
UID:260819Se34eyUGaE-KRFrVMa19AQ
DESCRIPTION:Expressions in Metal In the Main Gallery\, Expressions in Meta
 l brings together nine Northern California artists who treat metal not as 
 a static material but as a living language. Curated by Vicky Kumpfer\, thi
 s exhibition highlights a range of contemporary practices rooted in metalw
 ork. Some artists forge\, cast\, or weld\, honoring the discipline's long 
 lineage of craftsmanship. Others push the material into unexpected territo
 ries\, experimenting with surface\, scale\, and form. Across the exhibitio
 n\, metal is bent\, stretched\, pierced\, patinated\, and even coaxed into
  gestures that contradict its reputation for hardness. What emerges is a c
 horus of works that carry the traces of heat\, pressure\, repetition\, and
  decision-marks that become expressive in themselves. These expressions re
 mind us that metal\, for all its industrial associations\, will record tou
 ch\, hold history\, and reflect the light around it. Expressions in Metal 
 invites viewers to consider how a material often associated with infrastru
 cture and industry can become a site of storytelling and imagination. In d
 oing so\, the exhibition honors the enduring dialogue between maker and ma
 terial-one forged through curiosity\, skill\, and the desire to transform 
 the elemental into the expressive. Participating Artists: Ray Degischer\, 
 James Ford Grant\, Byron B. Kim\, Sean Paul Lorentz\, Michael McGinnis\, M
 onty Monty\, Martin Munsun\, J. Nick Taylor\, Shoji Uemura Exhibition Date
 s: July 23 - August 29\, 2026 Opening Reception: Thursday\, July 23\, 5:30
 -7:30pm  RSVP HERE This exhibition celebrates the depth and range of conte
 mporary metalwork\, featuring artists who forge\, cast\, weld\, and experi
 ment with contrasting materials to transform industrial elements into expr
 essive works of art.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/expressions-in-metal-exhibition/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
