BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bill Kirchen/Nina Gerber & Back pOrchEstra Peacetown concert Wed A
 ug 26 5p
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T200000
UID:260820lFV8i6J4bk-PchNrN9l8tA
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra: American Roots music at Peacetown's Ives Park
  concert series opening for me ole band-mate Bill Kirchen \\(The Moonlight
 ers & Commander Cody\\) and his Austin TX Trio plus Nina Gerber\n\nWed\, A
 ug 26 5:00-6:00\, Outdoors at 7400 Willow St\, Sebastopol\, CA 95472\n\nBi
 ll & Nina at 6:30-8:00 pm\n\nSee https://www.peacetown.org/summer-series-2
 026/2026/8/26/back-porchestra\n\n...and http://www.BackPorchEstra.com/show
 s.html\n\nand https://www.billkirchen.com\n\nBack pOrchEstra is Tim Eschli
 man \\(Etta James\, Commander Cody & His Western Airmen\, New Copasetics\\
 ) on vocals & resonator guitar\, Bowen Brown \\(John Lee Hooker\, Tommy Ca
 stro\, Rhythmtown-Jive\\) on drums\, Candy Girard \\(Delaney Bramlet\, Cli
 nt Black\, with Jerry Garcia on his album “Cats Down Under the Stars”\
 \) on violin\, Jen Rund \\(Lumination\\) on bass\, Steve Black on guitar a
 nd special Guest Kathy Kennedy on vocals.\n\nWe have a new single out!: ht
 tps://orcd.co/7jjvmmx ... "What Does Your Heart Say?" - a Breez west coast
  rock\, a hopeful idealistic Americana love song duet.\n\nPrevious Back pO
 rchEstra single: https://orcd.co/lxz1l6v "I'm Wild About My Lovin'"\, ... 
 celebrating the new "Stories In The Heart" album\, hear it all now!: https
 ://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\n"The guitars slam like saloon doors\, the violin tra
 ces lines that oscillate between melancholy and jubilation\, the rhythm se
 ction moves forward with a tranquil groove that never rushes but never fal
 ters... Back pOrchEstra delivers a luminous\, earthy\, profoundly human re
 cord. An album that makes you want to sit on a porch\, watch the sunset\, 
 and let the stories do their work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zicazine\n\n"Stor
 ies In The Heart\, retaining the charm inherent in this "retro" sound-musi
 c that feels more relevant today than ever before-and serving as a testame
 nt to the richness of the musical community in San Francisco and the Bay A
 rea. The album confirms his mastery of a wide array of genres\, effectivel
 y serving as a musical roadmap of American music... spanning blues\, Ameri
 cana\, country\, rock 'n' roll\, and rock-but even more so with their indi
 e\, rockabilly\, Tex-Mex\, 1920s-style Cajun\, zydeco\, New Orleans\, West
 ern swing\, and neo-Motown sounds.... magnificent songs with a vintage\, r
 etro flair\, featuring excellent compositions characterized by fluid lines
  that never lose their rhythm and evoke vivid imagery. With this new album
  Back pOrchEstra achieves-in perfect style-a homespun\, familiar \\("downh
 ome"\\) sound that reconciles us with the fine music of a bygone era." \\(
 translated from Italian\\) - Aldo Pedron\, Mescalina.it\n\nBack Porchestra
 's "Stories In the Heart": The opener\, 'Ever Think About It' is a Motown 
 flavored Northern soul-styled stomper\, though the violin solo is a little
  unexpected. The vocal is just a little low in the mix too but maybe that 
 just adds to the feel. No\, this hasn't come out of some obscure Detroit b
 asement studio\; these guys are from the San Francisco Bay Area! Perhaps l
 ess unexpected then is the imaginatively-rearranged version of Jim Jackson
 's 'I'm About My Lovin' bringing to mind Dan Hicks And His Hot Licks\, fro
 m the same area and who played a wide variety of rootsy music \\(mainly\\)
  from the '20s to the '40s. Back Porchestra make things even more eclectic
  adding a couple or later decades and a global base to the formula. Blg Al
  Anderson / Stephen Bruton's composition 'I Ain't Ever Slown Down'\, trans
 formed into an appropriately driving more or less straight Cajun number\, 
 with Candy Girard's violin playing really rather wonderful \\(as it is thr
 oughout\\). - Norman Darwen\, BITS - Blues In The South\, March 2026\, Exm
 outh\, UK\n\nBack pOrchEstra is a compact Shelter-in-Place-inspired musica
 l combo ....going back to the basics... Formed for the first time the lock
 ed-down summer of 2020. The band draws from new original material as well 
 as reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill B
 roonzy\, Bob Wills\, Bobby Charles ...even Christmas Jug Band tunes\n\n...
  check out the "Dusty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...
 a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis
  and Sid Page....\n\nThe previous single\, the Neo-Motown/Levon Helm style
  "Ever Think About It\," is here: https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, a
 nd USB-Music Cards available all over\, including https://www.globerecords
 .com\n\nmore at... https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://bac
 kporchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list
 =PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/b
 ackporchestra.bsky.social\n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/b
 ackporchestra\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nIns
 tagram: https://www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\n\\#rootsrock\n\n\\#am
 ericanrootsmusic\n\n\\#americanamusic\n\n\\#rockabillymusic\n\n\\#twangygu
 itar\n\n\\#backporchestra\n\n\\#acousticmusic\n\n\\#adultalbumalternative\
 n\n\\#singersongwriter\n\n\\#folkmusic\n\n\\#folkrock
LOCATION:Ives park
URL:https://www.peacetown.org/summer-series-2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ask E. Jean Screening for Sonoma County NOW!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T203000
UID:260820eplx3a7r-0yFlnzBFzQaWQ
DESCRIPTION:National Women's Equality Day special showing! "Ask E. Jean\,"
  the thrilling story of E. Jean Carroll’s life\, from her early days as 
 Miss Cheerleader USA to her rise as a trailblazing journalist\, author\, a
 nd beloved advice columnist. Carroll broke barriers as the first female ed
 itor at Esquire\, Playboy\, and Outside\, helping to redefine women’s ro
 les in media with her sharp wit and fearless voice. In recent years\, she 
 reignited public discourse by standing up to power\, becoming the only wom
 an to beat Donald Trump twice in court \\(now under attack again\\)\, and 
 sparking a national conversation about truth\, accountability\, and resili
 ence. A portrait of an indomitable woman who proved it’s never too late 
 to reclaim your voice\, rewrite your story\, and change the world. This ev
 ent is a fundraiser for Sonoma County NOW. Come\, join us!
LOCATION:The Rialto Cinemas Sebastopol
URL:https://rialtocinemas.com/coming-soon/ask-e-jean-seb/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
