BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Event: Pressing Matters by Alan Ramey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T180000
UID:260808ABK8zKtiT06caKoDgM_cCA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with Alan Ramer\, author of Pressi
 ng Matters. This event is free\, but we appreciate your RSVP below so we c
 an plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK Pressing Matters covers the bi
 g debates of wine - all the issues that winemakers and sommeliers tend to 
 disagree on. The book addresses the causal factors of terroir\, organic an
 d biodynamic farming\, old world vs. new world regional rules\, how signif
 icant the impact of climate change is on wine typicity\, how to define win
 e quality and determine the value of wine as well as the definitional ques
 tions and pros and cons of naturalness in wine.  The result of exhaustive 
 literature reviews and around a hundred interviews\, it is a novel angle t
 hrough which to approach wine\, ensuring that polar opposite points of vie
 w are heard out. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Alan Ramey is Co-President and co-owner 
 of Ramey Wine Cellars. Alan has trained in all aspects of the winery\, fro
 m the cellar to winemaking\, and works in all areas of the winery. Alan ap
 prenticed at Veramonte in Chile and Domaine Méo-Camuzet in Burgundy and c
 ompeted on the blind tasting team for the University of Cambridge. He curr
 ently serves on the Board of the California Wine Institute. He is the wine
 maker for Curious Ground\, a new project that attempts to rethink the Coun
 ty of Sonoma\, developing a blend that typifies what the region can become
 . Preferred Pronouns: he/him
LOCATION:Decant Bottle Shop & Bar (Napa Valley)
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1610175360706029/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
