BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley Games X and Helen's 50th featuring New Monsoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T170000
UID:26081922NOP6zrFkKC5SZPmXzhNA
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, we are thrilled to celebrate Valley Games X\, t
 he tenth anniversary of this one-of-a-kind event that could only happen h
 ere in the San Geronimo Valley.\n\nPart Olympics\, part block party\, and 
 entirely Valley-style\, the Valley Games have become one of the Community 
 Center’s most beloved traditions — bringing together neighbors of all 
 ages for a day of friendly competition\, laughter\, teamwork\, and unforge
 ttable community memories.\n\nHeld on Saturday\, August 29\, Valley Games 
 X is a family-friendly event where Valley villages compete in Olympic-styl
 e games for glory across a wildly entertaining lineup of events\, includin
 g Cornhole\, Hacky Sack\, Ping Pong\, Chess\, Baking\, an Obstacle Course\
 , Basketball Hot Spot\, and more.\n\nRepresenting villages from across the
  Valley\, teams including the Lagunitas Lightning\, Forest Knolls Trolls\,
  San Geronimo Running Salmon\, Woodacre Wild Turkeys\, Nicasio Newts\, and
  the Townies will come together for a full day of camaraderie\, community 
 spirit\, and good-natured rivalry.\n\nNew to the Valley Games? It’s easy
  to join the fun. Teams are made up based on the village you live in — o
 r identify with — so simply sign yourself or your family up\, and we’l
 l place you on your village team the day of the event.\n\nAs Valley Games 
 X marks ten years of community fun\, this year’s celebration also honors
  someone who has helped shape the spirit behind the event from the very be
 ginning: the Community Center’s own Helen Ferlino. To top off the festiv
 ities\, beloved Bay Area band New Monsoon will rock the Community Center
  Courtyard for an afternoon birthday celebration.\n\nLocation : Lagunitas 
 Middle School Campus\n\n10am - Registration Opens - Middle School Amphithe
 ater\n\n10am - Pancake Breakfast begins - LOFT\n\n11am - Opening Ceremonie
 s & Village Cheer Parade\n\n11:30am - Games Begin\n\n1:30pm - Games Close\
 n\nLocation: San Geronimo Valley Community Center Courtyard\n\n1:45pm - Fi
 nale - Village Freeze Dance\n\n2:00pm - Awards and Closing Ceremonies\n\n3
 :00pm - New Monsoon Concert in the Courtyard
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sgvperformingarts.eventcalendarapp.com/valley-games-featuring-
 new-monsoon
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mercy's Elevated Terrariums: Carnivorous Bog Workshop with Ladybir
 ds Flora
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T220000
UID:260817goUNzd3VKkKWspkQDtbXTw
DESCRIPTION:Join us at The Lounge at Mercy for a unique hands-on plant exp
 erience in partnership with Ladybirds Flora & Adornments! Spend an afterno
 on creating your own carnivorous bog garden while learning about these fas
 cinating plants and designing a one-of-a-kind living piece of art.\n\nDuri
 ng this approximately 2-hour workshop\, guests will build and customize th
 eir own carnivorous bog garden using vintage glass containers\, specialty 
 potting mix\, decorative elements\, and a selection of unique carnivorous 
 plants.\n\nChoose your garden size:\n\nMini Bog Garden — $75\n\nVintage 
 glass container\n\nCustom carnivorous potting mix\n\nDecorative rocks and 
 miniatures\n\n1 carnivorous plant\n\nLarge Bog Garden — $100\n\nVintage 
 glass container\n\nCustom carnivorous potting mix\n\nDecorative rocks and 
 miniatures\n\n3 carnivorous plants\n\nGuests will choose from a variety of
  carnivorous plants\, including:\n\n🌱 Pinguicula \\(Butterworts\\)\n\n
 🌱 Sundews\n\n🌱 Sarracenia\n\n🌱 Venus Flytraps\n\nAll tools\, mate
 rials\, and supplies are provided—just bring your creativity! Ladybirds 
 Flora & Adornments will guide you through the process and share tips for c
 aring for your new carnivorous plant creation at home.\n\nEach garden will
  be completely unique\, featuring a vintage glass vessel selected from a c
 urated collection of one-of-a-kind containers\, along with your choice of 
 plants and decorative accents.\n\nWhether you’re a seasoned plant lover 
 or simply looking for a fun and creative experience\, this workshop is the
  perfect way to spend an afternoon crafting\, connecting\, and bringing ho
 me something truly special.\n\nAbout Ladybirds Flora & Adornments\n\nBased
  in Cotati\, Ladybirds Flora & Adornments creates unique botanical experie
 nces and handcrafted plant designs inspired by nature\, creativity\, and c
 uriosity. Their popular terrarium workshops have delighted guests througho
 ut the community\, and they’re excited to bring this brand-new carnivoro
 us bog garden experience to The Lounge at Mercy.\n\nDate & Time\n\nDate: S
 unday\, August 30\, 2026\n\nTime: 12:00 - 3:00 PM\n\nWhat’s Included\n\n
 All tools\, materials\, and supplies are provided—just bring your creati
 vity! \n\nTicket Tiers\n\nMini Bog Garden — $75: Includes a vintage gla
 ss container\, custom carnivorous potting mix\, decorative rocks and minia
 tures\, 1 carnivorous plant \\(choose from a selection of pinguiculas\, su
 ndews\, sarracenia\, and flytraps\\)\, and some infused treats from Big Pe
 te's.\n\nLarge Bog Garden — $100: Includes a vintage glass container\, c
 ustom carnivorous potting mix\, decorative rocks and miniatures\, 3 carniv
 orous plants \\(choose from a selection of pinguiculas\, sundews\, sarrace
 nia\, and flytraps\\)\, and some infused treats from Big Pete's.\n\n21\\+ 
 Only | DCC \\# C12-0000420-LIC\n\nEvent Terms & Conditions\n\nThis event i
 s 21\\+ only. Valid government-issued ID is required for entry. By attendi
 ng this event at the Mercy Wellness Lounge\, you acknowledge that photogra
 phy and video recording may take place. Images and footage may be used by 
 Mercy Wellness for marketing and promotional purposes across various chann
 els\, without compensation. Tickets are non-refundable unless otherwise st
 ated. Event details\, timing\, or programming are subject to change.\n\nCa
 nnabis consumption is limited to designated areas and must comply with all
  applicable local and state regulations. Please consume responsibly.\n\nBy
  entering the venue\, you agree to comply with all house rules and venue p
 olicies.
LOCATION:The Lounge at Mercy
URL:https://eventhi.io/events/mercys-elevated-terrariums-carnivorous-bog-w
 orkshop-with-ladybirds-flora-14883
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qi Gong at Barbieri Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T230000
UID:260817_5mJsBUTxkml_VsxORAn4Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an hour of movement. Qi Gong (pronounced "chee gon
 g") is a gentle practice of movement\, breathing\, intention and mindfulne
 ss. Think of it as meditation in motion. The movements are simple and easy
  to learn. Everything can be adapted for a variety of abilities. All are w
 elcome...no experience necessary. You'll leave class feeling less stress a
 nd more of your inner vitality. Classes taughy by Marianne Benforado is a 
 licensed acupuncturist and certified Holden Qi Gong teacher. Students desc
 ribe her classes as welcoming and down to earth with good vibes sprinkled 
 on top. Drop in anytime it works for your schedule.
LOCATION:Barbieri Park 
URL:https://feelbetteracu.com/events/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
