BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Walk on the Wild Side - The World of Crepuscular and Nocturnal Wil
 dlife
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T210000
UID:260722qF7Fe7nNTEWfdtFCFQh6Fg
DESCRIPTION:Experience Jack London State Historic Park in a whole new way 
 during Walk on the Wild Side\, a guided evening hike that reveals the fasc
 inating world of the park’s crepuscular and nocturnal wildlife.\n\nAs th
 e sun begins to set and the landscape transforms\, participants will take 
 a moderate-paced hike along park trails\, stopping periodically to learn a
 bout the animals that become more active as daylight fades. Along the way\
 , a park naturalist will share insights into the behaviors\, habitats\, an
 d adaptations of the wildlife that thrive during the evening hours.\n\nThi
 s educational hike offers a unique opportunity to experience the park’s 
 sights and sounds as day transitions to night\, while gaining a deeper app
 reciation for the wildlife of Jack London State Historic Park.\n\nThis eve
 nt includes an approximately 3.25-mile round-trip hike and is considered m
 oderate in difficulty.  This hike is recommended for participants ages 12
  and older. All minors under the age of 18 must be accompanied by an adult
 .  Please note that pet dogs \\(non-service animals\\) are not permitted 
 on backcountry trails in order to protect wildlife.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/walk-on-the-wild-side/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
