BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:If You Give A Mouse A Cookie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T120000
UID:260819fnb94QLy5kaPUtat8c_nyA
DESCRIPTION:With a bag of cookies and a good spot in the yard to read his 
 comic book\, Boy was ready for a perfectly peaceful day. But then... Mouse
  came. He may be adorable\, but he's full of questions. And energy. And he
 's hungry. What can Boy do but give Mouse a cookie? Wouldn't you do the sa
 me thing? But if you give a mouse a cookie\, he's going to want a glass of
  milk...\n\nJody Davidson's adaptation\, based on the books by Laura Joffe
  Numeroff\, is a mayhem- and mishap-filled joyride for all audiences.\n\nS
 how details\n\nAuthors: Adapted by Jody Davidson\, based on the books by L
 aura Joffe Numeroff\n\nLocation: Cinnabar Theater Studio Space\, 2200 Peta
 luma Blvd N.\, Suite 700\, Petaluma\n\nPerformance dates: Sat Aug 22 \\(11
 am & 2pm\\)\, Sun Aug 23 \\(11am\\)\, Sat Aug 29 \\(11am & 2pm\\)\, Sun Au
 g 30 \\(11am\\)\n\nEstimated run time: 60 minutes\n\nRecommended for ages 
 3\\+. Children under 3 are welcome to attend at the discretion of their pa
 rent or caregiver. You know your child best! If your little one is ready f
 or a live theater experience\, we’d love to have them join the adventure
 .\n\nTickets: https://cinnabartheater.org/show/mouseacookie/
LOCATION:Cinnabar Studio Space at the Petaluma Village Premium Outlets #70
 0
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/mouseacookie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tim Flannery & Tim Flannery and the Lunatic Fringe & Jake Peavy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260831T000000
UID:260819QfAe6R80kkCeQNFsDIDgAw
DESCRIPTION:He is one of the enduring hard men of professional sports\, lo
 gging 34 of his 55 years with professional baseball. Of those years\, he h
 as spent a jaw-dropping 25 on the hallowed fields of the Major Leagues as 
 both a hard-charging player and a steely-eyed field general. He has been t
 o the World Series four times- once as a player and three times as a coach
 \, finally wrapping his battered\, dusty hands around the World Series Tro
 phy in 2010...and yet again in 2012 and 2014. Impressive credentials for a
 ny man\, but here's the thing- baseball is only a part of his story.	  He 
 is also a prolific and talented songwriter. That's right- this ferociously
  hard-working baseball legend is also an award-nominated musician who regu
 larly packs venues across the globe. He is a seasoned fingerstyle legend o
 f Americana music with a gift for crafting potent\, resonant songs and del
 ivering energetic\, emotional live shows.   His name is Tim Flannery and h
 e is writing some of the most gorgeous acoustic music to roll out of Calif
 ornia since the halcyon days of the Seventies folk explosion.  "Flan\," as
  he's known to family\, friends and players\, started playing baseball as 
 a kid and its hold on him has never loosened. As a player for his hometown
  San Diego Padres\, each season would begin with Tim's manager cautioning 
 him that his position would likely go to someone younger\, faster or more 
 gifted. A warrior to the core\, Flan distilled such negativity into furiou
 s motivation\, out-running\, out-gunning and out-hustling every guy on the
  team to secure his spot on the roster. Unsurprisingly\, his relentless wo
 rk ethic and fearless playing style made him a fan favorite and to this da
 y\, he is a much-beloved icon from the surf breaks of Oceanside\, Californ
 ia to the furthest tip of Mexico's Baja Peninsula.  When his playing caree
 r came to a close\, Flan took to coaching with the same passion and savvy 
 that propelled him to such auspicious heights as a player. He moved from t
 he minor league system back into the Majors as a third base coach for the 
 Padres\, and in 2008 he took over third base coaching duties for the San F
 rancisco Giants\, where he patrolled the left side of the field like a wol
 f\, managing the team's offensive attack with equal measures of strategy a
 nd pure guts. Flan announced his retirement from baseball shortly after th
 e San Francisco Giants earned their third World Series championship in 5 y
 ears.   Tim has spent the majority of his life on the road\, balancing his
  career and his creative drive with the love of his wife and three childre
 n. His music explores the depths of emotion that only loneliness and solit
 ude can reveal\, as well as the profound emotional highs unlocked in a gol
 den surfing session or in the majesty of a star-spangled sky from a back p
 orch in Kentucky.  Flan's music enjoys radio support across the planet\, f
 rom the shores of Ireland to beach towns up and down the California coast.
  He is routinely supported by an obscenely talented band and he has been j
 oined onstage by the likes of Jackson Browne\, Bruce Hornsby\, Garth Brook
 s and Jimmy Buffet. With a voice as smooth as Kentucky bourbon and heart w
 orn on both sleeves\, Flan's concerts ebb and flow with brilliant melodies
 \, soaring harmonies and themes of love\, travel and connecting with the G
 reat Spirit. And of course\, he sings about baseball. Whalebone Records...
 .Dont bone us\, we will bone you.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1038049705?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
