UID:260812Twqh2deZj0GIDJRruAAqMQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a community walk with Social Wellness Society\n\nJ
 oin us for a community walk through the neighborhood with Social Wellness 
 Society\, departing from and returning to The Courtyard at Montgomery Vill
 age. Afterward\, we invite you to explore the property with your wellness 
 passport and enjoy merchant incentives\, crafts\, wellness activities\, fr
 ee samples\, a DJ\, a flower photo wall\, and more! Plus\, every attendee 
 receives a goodie bag to take home.\n\nHow the Wellness Passport works: Wh
 en you arrive\, you'll receive a passport filled with fun activities and t
 asks to complete around the property\, each one earning you a stamp. Colle
 ct at least half of the stamps in your passport for a chance to enter our 
 giveaway for one of four $200 gift cards to the shop or restaurant of your
  choice at Montgomery Village.\n\nBy registering and attending this class\
 , you acknowledge that you have read and understand this Release and Waive
 r and accept and agree to the terms and provisions contained in this Relea
 se and Waiver.\n\nWe'll meet in The Courtyard at 10am and depart for our w
 alk shortly after.\n\nThis outdoor event will start and end atThe Courtyar
 d\, located between Salt & Straw \\(700 Village Court\\) and Monti's \\(71
 4 Village Court\\). Please wear layers\, sunscreen and don't forget your s
 unglasses and a water bottle!\n\nStrollers and dogs are welcome!
LOCATION:Montgomery Village Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/wellness-weekend-3/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wreckless Strangers at the Rio Nido Roadhouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T180000
UID:260812Joqpu4bi6UqnVKjcN-duDw
DESCRIPTION:After bringing their Ameri-Cali Soul sound to Littleton\, CO\,
  and Jackson Hole\, WY\, Wreckless Strangers return home for a summer run 
 of performances in the North Bay\, while continuing to build momentum with
  national radio airplay and a climb up the Top 50 Americana and AAA Single
 s charts. The band will perform at **Live on the Avenue** in **San Anse
 lmo** on **August 22**\, the **Old Western Saloon** in **Point Reyes 
 Station** on **August 28**\, and the **Rio Nido Roadhouse** on **Augu
 st 30.**\n\nWith ***Dirty Souls***\, Wreckless Strangers return to their 
 rock-and-roll roots\, delivering their rawest and most visceral studio eff
 ort to date. The six-song collection channels the arena rock spirit of the
  ’70s and ’80s that shaped the band’s earliest influences while brin
 ging a fresh\, modern edge to the sound. The first single\,**"Dirty Soul\,
 "** released January 23\, is receiving national airplay and is available 
 on major streaming platforms. The band released the full album on March 27
 .
LOCATION:Rio Nido Roadhouse
URL:https://rionidoroadhouse.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talk: Cnopius Field - Sebastopol's First Airfield (1925-19
 42)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T160000
UID:260810iqTCe_lKUE-rd7hOrnm_dQ
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that in 1925\, Sebastopol had its own nationally 
 recognized airfield? Learn about this piece of unique history at a free ta
 lk at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts on Sunday\, August 30th.  The ai
 rfield was the first in Sonoma County\, long before the Charles M. Schultz
 -Sonoma County Airport. It played a major role in the barnstorming era of 
 the 1910s-1930s and was a lively hub for early aviation events\, stunt fly
 ing\, and community gatherings. Gary Greenough will share the colorful and
  fascinating history of when Sebastopol was a flying hub. This 1-hour tal
 k is a project from the Western Sonoma County Historical Society. It will 
 be preceded by a short update by the society board about what is happening
  at the Historical Society\, Luther Burbank Experiment Farm\, and West Cou
 nty Museum. The event is free and open to the public.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.wschs.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Japanese Papermaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T160000
UID:260808gzEjK5XVyEGKoCk1N9aQaQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, August 29\, 2026 2:00 PM – 5:00 PM Su
 nday\, August 30\, 2026 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nEx
 perience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Bilingual\, Fiber Arts\,
  Printmaking\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n$180 – Registration Cost $
 25 – Materials Fee $205 – Total Registration Cost\n\nIn this workshop\
 , students will be introduced to the process of making Japanese paper. Jap
 anese paper\, often incorrectly referred to as rice paper\, is known for i
 ts great strength while appearing delicate and gossamer-thin. In this work
 shop\, students will learn the basics of preparing their own fiber\, hand 
 beating\, and forming sheets in the traditional nagashizuki method. Studen
 ts will take home wet sheets to dry at home with instructions.Please be aw
 are that papermaking is a wet activity –  wear clothing and shoes that 
 can get wet. Class involves some physical activity\, including standing an
 d arm movements. All supplies are provided through the materials fee. La m
 aestra habla español.Note: Please bring a bag lunch on Sunday.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/japanese-papermaking/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
