 Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistrati
 on Cost:\n\n$320\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:
 \n\n$320\n\nIn this 4 session intensive\, students will create work for a 
 soda firing while learning the history and chemistry of atmospheric Soda. 
 Each session there will be demos and assignments that will lend to intenti
 onal and experimental decisions on the objects we make for the firing. We 
 will make tests in clay material\, slips\, glazes\, experiment in wadding\
 , and placements in the kiln. During class there will be lectures on the c
 hemistry of clay and of soda firing as well as its history\, application\,
  and experiments within the field. This class is about learning how to exp
 lore what soda can do.During the 4 weeks each student will create one cubi
 c foot of work to be bisqued and then fired in the soda kiln. The firing 
 will be two full days of activity\, with students applying the lessons lea
 rned in class to the wadding and loading of the kiln and lighting the kiln
 . Students will learn how to plan a gas kiln schedule\, use a kiln log\, a
 ssess a kilns needs\, and successfully fire off a kiln. Students will lear
 n how to spray soda and how to maintain the kiln and her accessories in or
 der to support Julia’s \\(our beloved soda kiln\\) longevity. This deep
  dive into soda will spark ideas and expand folx knowledge on kilns\, firi
 ng\, and making in clay.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/deep-dive-into-soda-firing-
 with-dan-clauson/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
