 s on homelessness as one of the region's most significant economic\, publi
 c safety\, humanitarian\, and quality-of-life challenges. The goal is to c
 reate a practical\, data-driven discussion around outcomes\, accountabilit
 y\, and effective solutions. We’ll gain a better understanding of where 
 resources are currently invested and what results those investments are pr
 oducing\, learn from successful models from other communities and regions\
 , and explore what changes could produce better outcomes for individuals e
 xperiencing homelessness\, taxpayers\, businesses\, and the broader commun
 ity. 8:15–9:00 Coffee\, Breakfast & Networking 9:00–10:30 Program feat
 uring Nolan Sullivan\, Health Services Agency Director\, County of Sonoma 
 and Sarah Fields\, Deputy Director\, Public Affairs | Housing Department\,
  City of San José Tickets $45 member | $55 non-member by August 26 $55 me
