BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London State Historic Park WILD Trail Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T090000
UID:2608034NavkZh_r0eRtx2K8EvPHA
DESCRIPTION:On Saturdays from Sept. 5 to Oct. 3\, Jack London State Histor
 ic Park’s WILD Trail Challenge returns for a third year.  This series o
 f five hikes covers every trail in the park for a total of 39.5 miles.  T
 he hikes increase in duration and/or difficulty each week.\n\nParticipants
  can sign up for individual hikes or do them all.\n\nThe price for each hi
 ke is $15.  The park entry fee of $15 per vehicle is waived for these hik
 es.  Those who sign up for all five hikes before Sept. 5 save 20 percent 
 and pay only $60.\n\nHike \\# 1 – Historic Trails\n\nSeptember 5\, 9 a.m
 .-12:30 p.m.  \n\nA great way to warm up. This hike explores the historic
  sites and trails of the park. Navigate both sides of the park to discover
  Jack London’s Beauty Ranch\, London Lake\, and the Wolf House ruins.\n\
 nEasy – moderate hike \\(approximately 4.5 miles roundtrip\\)\n\nHike \\
 # 2 – Ancient Redwood\n\nSeptember 12\, 9 a.m.-1 p.m.   \n\nMeander th
 rough the redwoods and sunny oak woodlands of the park’s three Bridge Tr
 ails \\(Upper\, Lower\, and Fallen\\). The journey leads to the majestic a
 ncient redwood\, fondly known as the Grandmother Tree.\n\nModerate hike \\
 (approximately 6 miles roundtrip\\)\n\nHike \\# 3 – Historic Orchard\n\n
 September 19\, 9 a.m.-1:30 p.m.   \n\nStart Location: Note that this hik
 e does not begin at Jack London State Historic Park\n\nSonoma Developmenta
 l Center\n\nArnold Dr\, Eldridge\, CA 95431\n\nStroll along the blue shore
 s of Fern Lake before reaching the Historic Orchard. Learn about the histo
 ry of the land and the fascinating fruit-bearing crops that thrive there.\
 n\nModerate – Difficult hike \\(approximately 7 miles roundtrip\\)\n\nHi
 ke \\# 4 – Ridge\n\nSeptember 26\, 9 a.m-3:30 p.m.   \n\nDetails: Hike
 rs will gain elevation and an appreciation for the diverse habitats found 
 within the park. They’ll also traverse part of the ever-growing Bay Area
  Ridge Trail.\n\nDifficult hike \\(approximately 12 miles roundtrip\\)\n\n
 Hike \\# 5 – Summit \n\nOctober 3\, 9 a.m.-2:30 p.m.     \n\nA trek
  to the park summit is the perfect way to complete the WILD Trail Challeng
 es.  Climb Sonoma Mountain to enjoy stunning views\, celebrate with fello
 w hikers\, and become a WILD One.\n\nDifficult hike \\(approximately 10 mi
 les roundtrip\\)
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/wild-trail-challenge-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apple U-Pick at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T113000
UID:260731B9o4WAY0xkCXk9RVDvPgaw
DESCRIPTION:**Our popular Apple U-Pick Experiences return for a second yea
 r!**\n\nExperience the magic of harvest season at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
 \, where you can hand-select the most flavorful Honeycrisp or Fuji apples 
 straight from our certified organic orchard.\n\nTimed entries from 8:30am.
  Last orchard entry at 11:30am.\n\nAdmission: $8 for adults\, $3 for child
 ren. Registration required.\n\nU-Pick apples: $4 per pound.\n\n**Apple U-P
 ick FAQs** \n\nDo I need a reservation? \n\nYes! Please reserve your tim
 e slot on our reservation site. Reservations help us ensure everyone has a
  wonderful experience without overcrowding.  \n\nCan I show up without a
  reservation? \n\nWe require reservations to maintain our capacity limit
 s and ensure everyone enjoys their visit to the fullest.  \n\nCan I canc
 el my reservation?  \n\nAbsolutely! You can cancel your reservation up 
 to 48 hours before your scheduled time by calling us at 707-823-3100. Plea
 se note that cancellations made less than 48 hours in advance will result 
 in forfeiture of the entrance fee. \n\nCan I bring my dog?  \n\nDogs a
 re not permitted in the orchard\, with the exception of service animals. T
 his policy helps ensure the safety and comfort of all our visitors. \n\nC
 an I bring a stroller into the orchard?  \n\nFor safety reasons\, strol
 lers aren't allowed in the orchard\, but you're welcome to leave yours at 
 the check-in area where it will be safe and waiting for you!  \n\nI requ
 ire mobility accommodations. Can I still pick apples in the orchard?  \n
 \nYes. Please call us on 707-823-3110 once you’re made a reservation and
  we can provide suitable transportation into our orchard.\n\nWhy is there 
 an entrance fee?  \n\nThe entrance fee helps us maintain our beautiful 
 orchard and keep our experienced staff on hand to ensure everyone has a sa
 fe and enjoyable experience. \n\nHow much are the apples?  \n\nOur del
 icious U-pick apples are $4.00 per pound.  \n\nWhat variety of apples wi
 ll we be harvesting?  \n\nYou'll be picking either Honeycrisp or Fuji a
 pples (depending on seasonal availability).  \n\nCan I harvest heirloom 
 apples?  \n\nWhile heirloom apples aren't available for U-pick\, we off
 er many wonderful heirloom varieties for purchase in our Farm Shop.  \n\
 nAre your apples organic?  \n\nYes\, all our apples are organically gro
 wn and certified annually by Oregon Tilth!
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/u-pick
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
