BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tomales Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T170000
UID:2608051onyyq6tiUydf1rwfBSGrA
DESCRIPTION:The Tomales Festival will be held at High Noon on Labor Day Su
 nday\, September 6th. Join us in the Community Park \\(in between the Cath
 olic church and the William Tell House\\) to celebrate with friends and ne
 ighbors. This year we're featuring music by the Blues Defenders\, plus fre
 sh oysters\, beer\, wine\, food\, and drink. Local arts and crafts\, plus 
 displays from local organizations and non-profits.\n\nThe festival is \\(a
 nd always has been\\) created\, organized\, and carried out by volunteers 
 from the local community. This local tradition has quite a history: it was
  the Swiss-Italian celebration from 1888 until 1994\, when it became Found
 er's Day and later the Tomales Festival. That's 138 years worth of parades
 \, picnics\, and parties. This event benefits the Tomales Town Hall\, whic
 h is a 501\\(c\\)3 non-profit community center.\n\nSpecial thanks to Kathr
 yn LeMieux for once again allowing us to use her whimsical cow painting as
  our festive logo. And thanks to our contributors. The Hog Island Oyster C
 ompany and The Marshall Store contributed the shellfish. Morris Distributi
 ng is providing our beer supply. Recology Sonoma/Marin is providing trash 
 containers and is donating garbage service. We are grateful to our sponsor
  Marin Agricultural Land Trust \\(MALT\\).\n\nSign ups for volunteers\, e
 xhibitors\, vendors\, and more right are currently available. Write to fes
 tival@TomalesTownHall.org or see the website: https://www.tomalestownhall.
 org/tomalesfest. Booth reservations end August 15th.
LOCATION:Tomales Community Park
URL:https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London and Japan: Connections Across the Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T110000
UID:260803oiYE_8Y460CpkUCcYvV97w
DESCRIPTION:As part of a series co-hosted by Jack London Park Partners and
  the Jack London Society\, this is a rare opportunity to hear distinguishe
 d scholars from Japan present their research exploring the lives and relat
 ionships that connected Jack London with Japanese immigrants in early twen
 tieth-century California.\n\nProfessor Takaharu Mori will explore Jack Lon
 don’s relationships with Japanese immigrants\, focusing on Yoshimatsu Na
 kata and Kanae Nagasawa\, a descendant of samurai and one of California’
 s most influential early winemakers at Fountain Grove Winery in Santa Rosa
 . Through their stories\, the presentation reveals the personal and cultur
 al connections that linked Jack London with members of the Japanese commun
 ity in Northern California.\n\nNagako Muto\, Ph.D.\, a scholar of classica
 l Japanese literature\, will examine the remarkable 1914 diary of Yoshimat
 su Nakata\, a Japanese immigrant who lived and worked closely with Jack Lo
 ndon. Nakata’s firsthand observations provide an intimate view of London
 ’s daily life\, physical challenges\, and interactions with California
 ’s legal and cultural landscape.\n\nProfessor Mori’s former student\, 
 Dr. Kaoru Nishihara\, will conclude the program with a brief presentation 
 highlighting her own research into Jack London’s changing views of Japan
  and the Japanese people.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-part-4/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T170000
UID:260803kvqWdrz1UEuBzXWR9LeJIg
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T140000
UID:260803Mx-La3JKC0GpQUA8KXHJuQ
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare \\(after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s
  name\\). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to qu
 estion it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the ca
 sh\, tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate
 –lie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drop
 s into many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that
  resonates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six
  actors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of S
 hakespeare's other plays-in-progress \\(one of which becomes the famous Ma
 cbeth.\\)
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mountain Regional Park\, Pythian 
 Rd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T110000
UID:260726b8o9SkNU-USrjqxxueTg6Q
DESCRIPTION:Shuttle also offered on Sunday\, September 6.\n\n**How 
 it works**: Every half hour\, our Shuttle will leave from either
  Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center (making a brief sto
 p at the Goodspeed parking lot) or Hood Mountain Regional Park
 ’s Pythian Rd parking lot (with a brief stop at the equestria
 n lot). Make a reservation to ride to the other end of the tr
 ail and begin your hike\, or hike and ride back. We recommend 
 riding first and hiking back to your car afterward– no worries
  about how long you take to finish your adventure. The hike sh
 ould take 3½ to 4½ hours depending on your pace\; the distanc
 e is about **7.4 miles one-way** with **approximately 2\,300ft of
  elevation gain**. \n\nBring at least 64 oz of water\, sun prot
 ection (the majority of the trail is exposed)\, a good paper ma
 p (some of the trail signs on Hood Mtn Regional Park are still
  damaged from the 2020 wildfire and trails might not be well m
 arked)\, and if desired\, hiking poles\, a friend\, and a lunch.
 \n\nIf you are riding from Sugarloaf\, the Goodspeed lot fills u
 p quickly. If it is full\, please park at the main lot and pi
 ck up the shuttle at the Visitor Center (you will have to hike
  a mile back to the main lot from the bottom of the canyon/Go
 odspeed lot). If the Hood Mt. Pythian Lot is full\, please park
  at the Equestrian Lot\, by the Hood House\, in Los Guilicos.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026sepsatshuttle
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
