BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Lyft and Cab Rides by Wells Call Injury Lawyers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260907T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260907T100000
UID:260813pCdAn_kclkC836O5W8WcMg
DESCRIPTION:According to the Annual Report of California DUI Management I
 nformation System\, of the total number of crash fatalities in 2018\, 32.1
 % were alcohol-related in California. We are committed to helping our comm
 unity not be a part of this statistic.\n\nWe pride ourselves on making our
  community safer and giving back to our neighbors as much as we can. That 
 is why this holiday season\, if you decide to go out and celebrate\, we wi
 ll pay for your cab ride home to ensure that you make it home safely.\n\nW
 e’d like to introduce a new community initiative: Free Lyft and Cab Ride
  Program to help reduce the number of drunk drivers on the road during the
  holidays. This holiday season\, if you decide to go and drink\, please ma
 ke the responsible choice to grab a ride home instead of getting behind th
 e wheel. We will reimburse you for your fare home\, so save that receipt!\
 n\nRead more about our Holiday Ride-Share Program below for full details.
  \n\nNote: Because of their track record on failing to protect women from
  sexual assault and their lack of regard for consumer rights\, we do not s
 upport Uber.\n\nHow it Works:\n\nThe program is simple. If you have been d
 rinking – take an Lyft or cab\, and you’ll get a reimbursement from us
 !\n\nWe want you home safe this holiday season.\n\nQualifying Holidays:\n\
 nSuper Bowl Sunday\n\nSt. Patrick’s Day\n\nCinco de Mayo\n\nIndependence
  Day\n\nLabor Day\n\nHalloween\n\nThanksgiving Eve & Day\n\nNew Year’s E
 ve & Day\n\nDetails to the Program:\n\nRide must be on Lyft or a cab \\(No
 t Uber\\)\n\nRides must be in Solano County\n\nRides must be taken between
  5 pm on the day of the holiday and 10 am the next morning.\n\nYou must be
  of legal drinking age to qualify \\(21 and over\\).\n\nValid for one\, on
 e-way ride to a safe destination.\n\nLimit one reimbursement per household
 .\n\nA maximum value of $25.00 anywhere within Solano County.\n\nThe maxim
 um value includes a tip of up to 10%. Anything above a 10% tip on the base
  fare will not be reimbursed.\n\nParticipation in this promotion is limite
 d to the first 25 submissions.\n\nWhen Will I Get My Reimbursement?\n\nWi
 thin 10 business days\, you must submit a copy of your receipt and photo I
 D via mail to our office. We will mail you a check for your reimbursement 
 of a qualifying submission within 30 days of the holiday.\n\nWells Call In
 jury Lawyers 1455 Oliver Rd \\#110 Fairfield\, CA 94534 707-414-3464 www.w
 ellscall.com/\n\nSubmissions are limited and will fill up fast\, so don’
 t delay submitting your reimbursement.
LOCATION:CA 94534
URL:https://www.wellscall.com/free-ride-share/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature at Work
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260907T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260907T113000
UID:260810zD51wQctQE61GEGN9-lGAQ
DESCRIPTION:This Labor Day\, join a naturalist-led exploration of the rema
 rkable work happening throughout the landscape at Jack London State Histor
 ic Park. \n\nFrom nature’s architects and engineers to recyclers\, poll
 inators\, and cleanup crews\, wildlife is constantly working behind the sc
 enes to keep the ecosystem thriving. Along the way\, explore the important
  work people do to care for this special place.\n\nThere is an extraordina
 ry amount of activity happening in nature\, much of it just beyond our not
 ice. This three-mile\, family-friendly program invites participants to slo
 w down\, look more closely\, and discover the many ways wildlife and peopl
 e contribute to a healthy landscape.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/nature-at-work/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
