UID:260820zXJj4ctjAEu_yu0JLUkZ3g
DESCRIPTION:Raised in the Bay Area\, DJ Cal has gained a reputation for do
 ing multi-genre set lists designed to move the crowds with a blend of Trap
 \, EDM\,Hip-Hop and Reggaeton music. He calls the city of Santa Rosa his h
 ome\, but you might’ve heard his mixes on-air across the nation \\(San F
 rancisco\, Las Vegas\, Orlando\, Palms Springs\, etc.\\). He currently hol
 ds a spot as a Mixshow DJ on Fresno California B95\, with Teezzy Radio\, L
 ast Call and Friday night street party. DJ CAL has several Bay Area and No
 rthern California venues under his belt and you can catch him performing a
 nd hanging out with the hottest names in music around the Bay. He also has
  created his own day party\, "Brunch Behavior" that has gained much popula
 rity in the North Bay. Also\, his work has been supported and featured by 
 various blogs\, websites and record pools\; DJ City\, MyMP3Pool\, BpmSupre
 me and SmashTheClub\, and more. DJ CAL has worked hard to make his own mar
 k in the music industry.
LOCATION:Perch + Plow
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108787165?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:macbitches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T210000
UID:260820lnx6gzohsU6SnNHt_gl12g
DESCRIPTION:“macbitches takes Shakespearean themes and grounds them in 
 a recognizable\, modern reality — a smarter\, theater-centered Mean Gir
 ls\, if you will. It’s funny\, sharp\, and unafraid to let women be comp
 licated.” - Jeanette Seisdedos\, director\n\nmacbitches takes a darkly 
 funny look at the toxic\, high-stakes world of university theater\, center
 ing on a freshman who unexpectedly lands the role of Lady Macbeth. The pla
 y centers on freshman acting major Hailey\, who unexpectedly scores the co
 veted role of Lady Macbeth. Her upperclassmen rivals immediately invite he
 r over to “celebrate.” As the Fireball and Svedka flow\, the young wom
 en interrogate their own ambitions as well as the power structures that ha
 ve shaped their education—and when the night spirals into violent and sh
 ocking acts of betrayal\, they come to learn that what’s done cannot be 
 undone.\n\n\\*Content Advisory: Strong profanity\, physical and psycholog
 ical violence\, heavy substance abuse and underage drinking\, discussions 
 of mental illness and sexual misconduct\, and themes of betrayal and suici
 de. Recommended for mature audiences 16+.\n\nWritten by Sophie McIntosh\n\
 nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos\n\nRunning Time: 90 minutes with no interm
 ission\n\nSeptember 4th\, 5th\, 6th\, \\*10th\, 11th\, 12th\, 13th\, 18th\
 , 19th\, 20th.\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 
 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\n Adults: $25\n\nStudent w/ID:
  $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performance:  Pay What You Can\n\nWri
 tten by Sophie McIntosh\n\nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Benefit for Walker Creek Music Camp - An Evening of American Roots
  Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T210000
UID:260820fg-WQPfTgUyFWx_JXKMCXw
DESCRIPTION:Walker Creek Music Camp Presents Teacher Concert Series V\n\nB
 enefit Concert Celebrating American Roots Music\n\nSEBASTOPOL\, CA — Wal
 ker Creek Music Camp presents Teacher Concert Series V – Benefit Concert
  celebrating the rich traditions and exciting future of American roots mus
 ic on Friday\, September 11\, 2026\, from 7:00–9:00 p.m. at the Sebastop
 ol Community Cultural Center\, 390 Morris Street\, Sebastopol.\n\nProceeds
  from the concert support Walker Creek Music Camp’s mission to provide w
 orld-class music education and access to traditional American roots music 
 for students of all ages. Audience members can look forward to an inspirin
 g evening of live music featuring celebrated WCMC faculty alumni showcasin
 g bluegrass\, old-time\, jazz\, swing and other forms of American roots mu
 sic.\n\nPerforming artists: Crying Uncle Bluegrass Band – Evie Ladin Ban
 d – Pacific Drive\n\nCrying Uncle Bluegrass Band – Widely recognized a
 s one of the most exciting young bands in acoustic music\, Crying Uncle B
 luegrass Band blends bluegrass\, Dawg music\, jazz\, and original composi
 tions with remarkable musicianship and youthful energy. Brothers Miles Qu
 ale \\(mandolin\, guitar\, vocals\\) and Teo Quale \\(fiddle\, guitar\,
  vocals\\) are joined by Andrew Osborn \\(bass\, vocals\\) and 2023 Nati
 onal Flat Pick Guitar Champion Ian Ly \\(guitar\, vocals\\)\, creating a
  fresh and innovative sound rooted in tradition.\n\nNamed the 2023 Intern
 ational Bluegrass Music Association Momentum Band of the Year\, the group 
 made its Grand Ole Opry debut in 2024 and was honored to perform at the 
 Bluegrass Music Hall of Fame's induction of their musical hero\, David Gri
 sman. Their performances have taken them to premier festivals across North
  America\, Europe\, and Asia\, earning a reputation as one of bluegrass mu
 sic's brightest rising stars.\n\n"Go and check out Crying Uncle! We dig wh
 at they are doing! The future of music is in good hands here!" — David 
 Grisman\n\nEvie Ladin Band – Banjo player\, singer\, songwriter\, percus
 sive dancer\, choreographer\, and square dance caller\, Evie Ladin is on
 e of the most dynamic and innovative voices in contemporary roots music. B
 lending old-time Appalachian traditions with influences from African Diasp
 ora music and dance\, her performances are rich in rhythm\, storytelling\,
  and joyful energy.\n\nA master of clawhammer banjo\, Evie's music has bee
 n featured everywhere from A Prairie Home Companion and Lincoln Center t
 o Hardly Strictly Bluegrass and Celtic Connections. Based in Oakland\, Cal
 ifornia\, she tours internationally with the Evie Ladin Band\, featuring
  Keith Terry \\(bass\, body percussion\, vocals\\) and Erik Pearson \\
 (guitar\, vocals\\). Together they create an exciting blend of old-time\, 
 folk\, and contemporary roots music. The band has released five acclaimed 
 albums of original "neo-traditional" music\, along with Riding the Rooste
 r\, a collection of traditional fiddle-banjo duets.\n\n"A natural entertai
 ner with a gift for infusing folk practices with contemporary verve." – 
 San Francisco Chronicle\n\nPacific Drive – Pacific Drive was born at Wal
 ker Creek Music Camp in 2015—at dances\, beside the pond\, and in late-n
 ight jam sessions that stretched well past midnight.\n\nThe band features 
 fiddler Dana Frankel\, mandolinist David Thiessen\, guitarist Jesse Fichma
 n \\(formerly of AJ Lee & Blue Summit\\)\, bassist Helen Foley\, and banjo
 ist Sam Reed. Lifelong friends who grew up in California’s bluegrass com
 munity\, they deliver hard-driving traditional bluegrass\, tight harmonies
 \, and the unmistakable chemistry of musicians who have played together si
 nce their teens.\n\nAbout Walker Creek Music Camp – Walker Creek Music C
 amp is a California nonprofit 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) corporation \\(EIN 99-3474
 773\\) dedicated to teaching\, preserving\, and celebrating American roots
  music traditions. Founded in 2013\, the camp welcomes students of all age
 s to experience its world-class music education program held twice each ye
 ar at the Walker Creek Ranch Conference Center\, just west of Petaluma.\n\
 nWalker Creek’s Music & More \\(M&M’s\\) youth program offers tuition-
 free instruction for children ages 6–13\, and also provides scholarships
  and work-trade opportunities that make music education accessible to all
 —ensuring that traditional music continues to thrive for generations to 
 come.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://walkercreekmusiccamp.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cheeseboard Workshop with Alli Keyser-Marti at Gold Ridge Organic 
 Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T133000
UID:260820_cxoz6RDIUyutBO8WmHJnw
DESCRIPTION:Join Gold Ridge Organic Farms' resident cheese expert\, Alli K
 eyser-Marti for an intimate hands-on cheeseboard workshop! Explore how to 
 create your own beautiful board\, showcasing a wide array of flavors\, tex
 tures\, and colors. Learn how to incorporate a variety of edible flowers a
 nd fresh herbs\, local honey\, apple cider syrup\, balsamic vinegar\, EVOO
 \, olives\, artisan bread\, crackers\, and dips to accompany the best loca
 l cheeses made by artisan producers from Sonoma County and beyond.\n\nAll 
 ingredients and materials included in ticket price. You'll get to take hom
 e your creation to share with friends and family.\n\nBuilding on a culinar
 y career starting in her teenage years\, in 2014 Alli Keyser-Marti fell in
  love with exploring the world of milk\, salt\, enzymes\, and microbes. He
 r cheese journey includes managing Cowgirl Creamery’s original Pt Reyes 
 shop\, overseeing the Oliver’s Market Stony Point cheese department\, as
  well as being awarded an ACEF Scholarship to attend the American Cheese S
 ociety's Portland conference in 2022\, where she successfully completed th
 e Certified Cheese Professional® exam. In 2025 Alli also became an ACS Ce
 rtified Cheese Sensory Evaluator® and judged cheese for the Good Food Awa
 rds. She has followed this passion from her backyard in California to smal
 l farms all over France\, rural Ohio\, roadside stands in Sardinia\, and f
 erries in Croatia. Most recently you’ll find her skillfully pairing chee
 se with olive oil and apple tastings at Gold Ridge Organic Farms\, as well
  as working on an apprenticeship with Applied Sensory for Olive Oil analys
 is and maintaining our organic certifications.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/615226/chee
 seboard-workshop-with-alli-keyser-marti-ccp-ccse
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Capo Creek Harvest Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T200000
UID:260815gqwckWZ0sEixhFkzA-z2uw
DESCRIPTION:This is a fantastic 2 day event so be sure to order the COMBO 
 ticket to get the best overall experience. The weekend starts with a Frida
 y (Sept 11)  welcome reception with food & wine at which time instruction
 s and supplies for grape picking will be distributed. At 5:00am the grape 
 pick begins as daylight breaks\, followed by our annual champagne breakfas
 t at dawn while processing & stomping grapes. After breaking for personal
  time\, the celebration continues with Harvest Dinner Saturday at 5:00pm. 
 The theme this year is **Out of This World**... think space\, astronauts\,
  aliens\, the future. Dress up is not mandatory but way more fun if you do
 . Prizes are awarded for character representation so joining in on the fun
  is encouraged. Ticket options include a HARVEST DINNER option without the
  winery experience.
LOCATION:Capo Creek Winery
URL:https://capocreekranch.com/product/26-harvest-combination/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jeffrey Halford & The Healers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T000000
UID:260813ho8Bb18Yv0Syxozz6c5HLQ
DESCRIPTION:Of the many marks of genius associated with rock n’ roll gre
 atness\, the knack for surrounding oneself with transformational talent lo
 oms especially large\, with The Rolling Stones being perhaps the most nota
 ble example. Jeffrey Halford treads a poetic rootsy path on his latest rel
 ease\, SOUL CRUSADE\, combining a bulletproof collection of songs inspired
  by gospel\, folk\, soul\, and blues\, with a formidable roster of musical
  contributors. The result is one of Halford’s most approachable and easy
 -grooving.\n\nHis latest album release\, SOUL CRUSADE\, is the follow-up t
 o the critically acclaimed record WEST TOWARDS SOUTH. The album came out i
 n Europe on Continental Song City\, debuted in September at \\#2\, and the
 n undisputedly reached \\#1 in October 2022 and stayed in the chart for fo
 ur months. \n\nJEFFREY HALFORD & THE HEALERS are gearing up for their eigh
 th European tour in September and October 2025\, bringing their signature 
 blend of raw rock ‘n’ roll\, country\, and soul back to the stage. But
  this tour isn’t just another run—it marks the 25th anniversary of KER
 OSENE\, the album \\(release date Friday\, August 29th\, 2025\\) that put 
 Halford on the map as a true Americana troubadour.
LOCATION:The Elephant In the Room
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108309641?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
