DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T210000
UID:260810ssbAOkCBd0uwxkogIjLi3Q
DESCRIPTION:Join Aeternum\, California's professional chamber choir\, for 
 a concert and wine reception in the Clos Pegase wine caves. Origins explor
 es the Renaissance’s greatest hits like Allegri’s Miserere\, Byrd’s 
 Mass for Five\, and more\, alongside their re-imagined works by today’s 
 most exciting living composers. \n\nProgram:\n\nHildegard von Bingen — 
 Ave generosa\n\nWilliam Byrd — Ave verum corpus\n\nRoderick Williams —
  Ave verum corpus Re-imagined\n\nWilliam Byrd — Kyrie from Mass for Five
  Voices\n\nRoxanna Panufnik — Kyrie After Byrd\n\nGregorio Allegri — M
 iserere mei\, Deus\n\nJames MacMillan — Miserere\n\n-Interval-\n\nWillia
 m Byrd — Ne irascaris\n\nNico Mulhy — Fallings\n\nGiovanni Pierluigi d
 a Palestrina — Stabat mater\n\nKerensa Briggs — Stabat mater\n\nMargar
 et Rizza — Ave generosa
LOCATION:Clos Pegase Wine Caves
URL:https://www.aeternumchoir.org/buy-tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:7 Minutes Max - Literary Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T200000
UID:260804jGNCOdGv1k6WOLFabvZLmA
DESCRIPTION:Bring your original poems\, prose or storytelling to our open 
 mic night!\n\nWe'll pick 7 performers from the hat - come share your work\
 n\nRead aloud or memorized - just keep it to 7 minutes or less\n\n2nd Frid
 ays of the month 7pm\n\nStories teach us about life\, about ourselves & ab
 out each other. Help to create west county’s newest storytelling communi
 ty. 7 Minutes Max is an evening of live stories\, poems\, or readings told
  in 7 minutes or less. Hilarious or sublime\, poignant and personal tales 
 told through the ancient oral tradition of storytelling\, this evening wil
 l be sure to move\, delight & intrigue you. This is an event for mature au
 diences & not intended for children. Interested storytellers will have a c
 hance to throw their name in the hat to present their story. Remember\, 7 
 minutes max! Notes allowed for readers.\n\n$10 GA\, $5 for OCA members. Pa
 y at the door. Storytellers will be selected randomly from willing partici
 pants.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/156962/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T193000
UID:2608037xCF74D0O0q4-ggzW8cDhA
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare \\(after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s
  name\\). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to qu
 estion it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the ca
 sh\, tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate
 –lie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drop
 s into many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that
  resonates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six
  actors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of S
 hakespeare's other plays-in-progress \\(one of which becomes the famous Ma
 cbeth.\\)
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T223000
UID:2608035_wBHHdKk0G1K4o9i8cE4Q
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
