DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T140000
UID:260820BlwddBhwCk6cW-Wxx1d_VA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Season: Food\, Community & Sustainability! Join 
 Cultivate Community Food Co-op and the JFK Library for a celebration of ou
 r local harvest! Whether you have a thriving backyard garden or just want 
 to learn more about eco-friendly living in Vallejo and Benicia\, there's s
 omething for everyone. This family-friendly event is free\, open to all ag
 es\, and packed with interactive learning.  Event Schedule: 11:15 am: Cook
 ing Demonstration - Cinnamon Apple Sauce by Executive Chef Andrea Quinn. F
 ree samples! 11:45 am: "How Food Co-ops Empower the Community" with Paula 
 Schnese\, President of Cultivate Community Food Co-op 12:15 pm: Workshop -
  How to Clean and Sharpen Garden Tools by Scott Dodson from Sustainable So
 lano. 12:45 pm: Cooking Demonstration - Sauerkraut\, by Master Fermenter I
 an Griffin. Free samples! 1:15 pm: Workshop - Truth & Soil Farm\, LLC: How
  to Make Lip Balm. Featured Highlights · The Community Share Table: Bring
  what you can\, take what you need! Share your backyard summer bounty\, ex
 tra seeds\, starter plants\, or garden tools\, and pick up some new green 
 treasures for free. · Live Culinary & Green Demonstrations: Watch and lea
 rn from local experts throughout the event! Catch two live cooking demonst
 rations \\(complete with free delicious samples\\) and gather practical ti
 ps for gardening and sustainable living. · Co-ops & Sustainability Spotli
 ght: Discover how community-led food co-ops empower neighborhoods\, protec
 t the environment\, and build sustainable local food networks. · Local Pa
 rtner Booths: Meet\, connect\, and chat with incredible organizations and 
 businesses dedicated to sustainability\, urban gardening\, and local food 
 security.
LOCATION:Vallejo John F. Kennedy Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17004453
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
