SUMMARY:Introduction to Reduction Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T130000
UID:2608229BD7c0CXyUexDiZQojXZ0g
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays Weekly · 4 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 5 – 
 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nP
 rintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nReg
 istration Cost:\n\n$195\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$225\n\nIn this special four-week workshop\, participants will explo
 re the unique art of reduction relief printmaking. Acclaimed guest artist\
 , Tomoko Murakami\, will demonstrate how to create multi-color prints from
  a single linoleum block. The main idea is to gradually carve away parts o
 f the block and print each new layer of color\, with each layer building o
 n the previous one. The course covers the entire process\, from designing 
 and planning\, to carving techniques\, inking\, registration\, and printin
 g with both hand and printing press methods. Participants will learn to ex
 plore the possibilities of color mixing and layering\, enabling students t
 o achieve intricate designs and a wide range of visual effects. You will g
 ain an understanding of the materials\, processes\, and innovations involv
 ed in this unique form of relief print printing!All levels are welcome\, i
 ncluding continuing linocut students. **Please note:** This class require
 s hand dexterity to maneuver the carving tool. Participants should feel co
 mfortable standing\, and using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-l
 inocut/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Collage Your Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T150000
UID:260821upvyltqVvkSrDOuLaMQUhw
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 12\, 2026 11:00 am to 3:00 pm\n\nLocation
 \n\nRoom 110\n\nCategory\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nExperience L
 evel\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n16+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$115\n\nMateria
 ls Fee:\n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$125\n\nJoin French-American
  collage artist Catherine Cruz for a special\, personalized workshop desig
 ned just for you! The word collage comes from the French verb coller\, mea
 ning “to glue\,” and is all about merging various materials to tell a 
 visual story. Much like our lives\, which are shaped by countless moments 
 and experiences\, collage pieces bring together fragments that reveal hidd
 en connections and untold narratives. In this class\, you’ll reflect on 
 what matters most to you and how that can be expressed through art. Cather
 ine will help you release the need for perfection and trust your creative 
 instincts. By the end of the workshop\, you’ll not only have a finished 
 artwork but also a deeper connection to your creative potential and a rene
 wed love for the art of collage. Some of the images featured on this page 
 show artwork created by students who have participated in Catherine’s pr
 evious workshops.\n\n**What You’ll learn**\n\nCreative ways to incorpora
 te your personal story in your art \n\nMethods for sourcing interesting c
 ollage papers\n\nTechniques for crafting textured\, multi-layered collages
 \n\nStrategies for refining your composition\n\n**Requirements**\n\nPlease
  bring your own papers to personalize your artwork like ephemera that repr
 esents your life or a certain period of time\, copies of photos\, old lett
 ers\, book pages\, papers from memorable experiences or travels\, or docum
 ents that hold meaning. If you’re not comfortable using these documents\
 , you should make laser color copies of them. You will not be able to use 
 anything printed on glossy paper or photo paper so it is best to make lase
 r copies of your photographs. Inkjet prints do not work with this process.
 \n\nParticipants must purchase and bring the following items – Instructo
 r will not provide panels for this class:\n\nOne 12”x12” cradled wood 
 panel\, either ¾” thick or 1 ½” thick – panel can be purchased loc
 ally at RileyStreet Art Supply or online at Blick.com – Do not use a can
 vas.\n\nApron or painting shirt\n\nNitrile gloves if you have sensitive sk
 in\n\nBrown bag lunch and beverage\n\nAny collage papers you would like to
  use. Please see website for supply list
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/collage-your-story/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
